			"color":"#432",
			"widgets_values":[
				"# Seedance 2.0 Image Reference Syntax Instructions\n## 1. Syntax Rules\nSeedance 2.0 supports precise reference to uploaded materials via the **@ + resource ID** format. It stably locks characters, products, backgrounds and motion references to ensure visual consistency, serving as the core syntax for digital human creation, product live-stream videos and scene restoration generation.\n\n## 2. Basic Reference Format\n1. Standard image reference syntax\n`@image + number`\nExamples:\n- First uploaded image：@image1\n- Second uploaded image：@image2\n- Third uploaded image：@image3\n\n2. Extended reference rules\nVideo reference：@video1\nAudio reference：@audio1\n\n## 3. Application Examples\n1. Lock real person / digital human character\n> Fix the character appearance with @image1, natural facial expressions and smooth movements\n\n2. Handheld product display for live commerce\n> @image1 is the virtual host, holding and displaying the product of @image2 with both hands, slowly rotating to show product details\n\n3. Fixed scene background\n> Adopt the scene environment of @image3, with unified style and high definition\n\n## 4. Usage Specifications\n1. The serial number strictly follows the **upload order**; the first uploaded image corresponds to `@image1`, and so on.\n2. Multiple images can be referenced in one prompt to jointly constrain characters, products and multiple elements.\n3. The reference syntax needs to be embedded in positive prompts with coherent semantics, and can be used with actions, composition and style descriptions.\n4. For real-person video generation, enable `real_person_mode: true` and combine with real-person image reference such as @image1 to improve generation stability.\n\n## 5. Incorrect & Correct Writing\n❌ Incorrect：@1、image1、@img1\n✅ Correct：@image1、@image2"
			],
